# RC5-GR1 — Generic bounded Eddy recovery supervisor
#
# Target: exact hardware-tested RC5 candidate after RS1 Phase 1
# Base candidate probe_eddy_current.py SHA256 before RS1:
# dcb78d4d7d5108236eca23a225e6e582e1b128419bf10c8a5b83cf8de346ced0
# Dependency:
#   patches/10_rc5_rs1_rapid_scan_lifecycle_guard.patch
#
# Design goals:
# - Prefer bounded automatic recovery for supported public Eddy-bearing commands.
# - Only the outermost supported command owns recovery/replay.
# - If M_Bamboo_Start_Sequence is active, it remains the outer recovery owner;
#   direct-command wrappers become transparent pass-throughs.
# - Never recover from I2C/bulk/lookahead/flush callbacks. Recovery begins only
#   after a normal command_error reaches the synchronous public-command owner.
# - One automatic recovery attempt per direct command invocation.
# - The failed operation is replayed from its beginning; partial mesh/QGL/ZCAL
#   output is never resumed or accepted.
# - No change to rapid-scan SAMPLE_TIME, path, speed, height, interpolation,
#   timestamping, or LDC query rate.
#
--- a/backend/probe_eddy_current.py
